 "press_quotes": [
  {
   "quote": "The hull designed by VPLP demonstrates efficiency with a smooth entry into the water, as the volume is only developed above the waterline.  From the flybridge, where the helm station is located, with the steering wheel in the center, visibility is good.",
   "source": "YACHT CLASS"
  },
  {
   "quote": "The Lagoon 51 is the latest flagship launched by Lagoon Catamarans.  The concept of this innovative boat is particularly geared toward sustainable development.",
   "source": "VOILES ET VOILIERS"
  },
  {
   "quote": "The Lagoon 51 marks an important step in the perpetual evolution of Lagoon.  With a long test period and increasingly advanced environmentally responsible technology, this sailboat has numerous attractive points.  Not to be overlooked are the fine seaworthy qualities and attractive layouts in this owner’s version.",
   "source": "BATEAUX.COM"
  },
  {
   "quote": "With the Lagoon 51, the number one on the international market of cruising catamarans innovates with a model distinguished by its comfort, its optimized flow of movement on board, and its fit and finish.  It is also the first production-model catamaran to integrate so many environmentally responsible solutions!",
   "source": "ACTUNAUTIQUE"
  },
  {
   "quote": "This Lagoon 51 is set up with around 2.7kW of solar panels, giving plenty of juice for running the windlass. In fact, it’s entirely self sufficient for power, despite a whopping 500l of fridge and freezer capacity, unless the aircon is used.",
   "source": "YACHTING WORLD"
  },
  {
   "quote": "With  a bright and inviting interior, numerous on-deck places to relax or socialize, good sailing manners, and a versatile array of layouts for couples, families or chartering, the Lagoon 51 does a number of things right.",
   "source": "CRUISING WORLD"
  },
  {
   "quote": "Lagoon has revealed imagery of the Iconic editions of the Lagoon 46 and 51 sailing catamarans, models that can both feature up to 12 berths. The Iconic option includes interior designs outfitted with ‘vibrant and pastel’ upholstery inspired by retro designs attributed to the 1980s.",
   "source": "YachtStyle"
  }
 ]
}
